./LOGBOOK.md:950:- DECISION: M0 uses fixed schema constants and unilateral local caps; nothing new on the wire beyond the existing `maxFrame` min-negotiation. Hello flag bit 1, feature bit 1, and message types `0x40–0x4F` reserved (unallocated) for an evidence-gated M3 limits exchange. Rationale: peer-advertised limits are unverifiable claims (local hard caps stay mandatory regardless), the datagram ceiling is HEV-pinned so negotiation has nothing to negotiate, and manifest-verified relay upload version-locks peer pairs. Full record: board outcome `TASK-260715-18owh7_decision.md`; awaiting review acceptance (proposed ADR-021).
./LOGBOOK.md:951:- FINDING: Pinned HEV caps UDP-in-TCP copy buffers at `UDP_BUF_SIZE = 1500` (`hev-socks5-udp.c:26`); `recvmmsg_tcp` returns `-1` (stream-fatal, not a drop) when `datlen > 1500 − addrlen` (`hev-socks5-udp.c:203-206`). With ADR-020 keeping HEV unmodified, the relay→client reply path physically cannot carry a UDP payload above 1481 bytes (IPv6). This, plus unfragmented 1500-MTU egress, fixes `maxUDPPayload = 1472` as a v1 wire constant; raising it is an HEV-fork decision, not a protocol negotiation.
./LOGBOOK.md:952:- DECISION: Baselines (all injectable, schema-owned floors/hard ceilings, fail-closed on out-of-range config): maxFrame [2048,65536] advertise 4096; maxAssociations 256 [1,1024]; per-assoc queue client 32KiB/relay 64KiB; aggregate/direction client 1MiB/relay 4MiB; control reserve 16/64KiB; DNS WRR 4:1; idle client 60s / relay 120s (RFC 4787 REQ-5 floor; client-first stagger shrinks crossed-expiry reopen race). `0x0005` split into violation (>1472, association-fatal) vs policy (lowered local cap, drop); `0x0006` edge-triggered per saturation episode.
./LOGBOOK.md:957:- MILESTONE: TASK-260715-111tde accepted → done. `TASK-260715-111tde_relay-binding-decision.md` is now the authoritative relay protocol v1 binding: schema/generated/handwritten ownership, deterministic regeneration + CI drift gates, bounded stream abstractions, dependency/license/FFI ceilings, and the full downstream consumer map. M2 protocol implementation (2azda7, 1y1g1u, 89h7cw, 516lhy, 1jvgcn, 1q7u14) is unblocked pending only the 18owh7 numeric-limit decision.
./LOGBOOK.md:958:- VERIFICATION: Wire contract byte-checked against `.spec/relay-protocol.md` (hello 12/16, envelope, message table, HEV payload — exact match); HEV `HDRLEN` 10/22/7+N and 248-byte domain cap confirmed via `.research/260720_pin-and-audit-hev-lwip-baseline.md:208-225`; SSH binding matches `Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift:1480-1527`; toolchain/license ceilings match accepted 3bdplx; all 32 spot-checked consumer-map task IDs exist; A0/32umrc unlinked per override; `task-board validate` clean; no product code modified.
./LOGBOOK.md:963:- OVERRIDE / ROUTING: The reviewer-accepted task override supersedes the 1510 stop-line and deliberately decouples this reusable wire contract from Gate A0 and TASK-260715-32umrc. Binding authority is the accepted ReluxTunnelCore boundary (TASK-260715-2nfz7w), cgo-free Go 1.26.5 relay toolchain (TASK-260715-3bdplx), candidate-neutral SSHExecChannel (TASK-260720-100wu6), and ADR-005/006. The obsolete A0/32umrc dependency edges are removed; those decisions remain outside the relay contract.
./LOGBOOK.md:964:- DECISION: Canonical JSON at `Protocol/Relay/relay-v1.schema.json` generates checked-in Swift/Go values only; handwritten Swift in `ReluxTunnelCore/RelayProtocol` and Go in `relay/internal/protocol` own behavior. `make relay-protocol-generate` is the sole regeneration command and `make relay-protocol-check` owns deterministic double-generation, drift/manual-edit failure, compilation, and schema-negative gates. No Swift/Go FFI or runtime schema parser is permitted.
./LOGBOOK.md:965:- DECISION: Build identity uses a separate bounded `relux-relay --identity --protocol 1` exec record matched to the signed manifest before `--stdio --protocol 1`; the fixed 12/16-byte v1 hello remains unchanged and framed stdout stays uncontaminated. DNS priority is a negotiated scheduling hint only. HEV `MSGLEN` is DATA length, `HDRLEN` includes the three-byte prefix, and domain wire length is capped at 248 by one-byte `HDRLEN`.
./LOGBOOK.md:1098:### 2220 — Four relay assets built; native runtime and budget gates remain external (TASK-260715-24icoz)
./LOGBOOK.md:1099:- IMPLEMENTATION: Added `relay-portable-assets` / `inspect-assets`, which requires a caller-owned total bundle budget and emits a path-free four-asset report only after exact layout/name, regular executable mode, raw format/machine, Go CPU metadata, linkage, minimum runtime, dynamic-library, debug-section, size, SHA-256, and privacy checks. An over-budget report is retained before the command fails; no default budget silently creates product policy.
./LOGBOOK.md:1100:- VERIFICATION: A detached clean worktree at `58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096` built exactly Darwin/Linux amd64/arm64 with pinned Go 1.26.5, `--require-clean`, release linker flags, protocol v1 identity `0.1.0`, and source epoch `1784656987`. The four files total 10,259,950 bytes and are retained in task outcome archive `TASK-260715-24icoz_portable-relay-assets.tar.gz`; each is mode 0755, stripped with no DWARF companion, and passed format/linkage/metadata/privacy inspection.
./LOGBOOK.md:1170:- MILESTONE: Go 1.26.5 relay toolchain decision reviewed and accepted; unblocks TASK-260715-1ccx3l, 1g9cyt, 32umrc and the M2 relay build with no open language/tooling question.
./LOGBOOK.md:1176:- DECISION: Implement `relux-relay` as a standard-library-only Go module pinned to official Go 1.26.5; build `linux/{amd64,arm64}` and `darwin/{amd64,arm64}` with `CGO_ENABLED=0`, exact output names, SPDX SBOMs, and a versioned JSON SHA-256 manifest.
./LOGBOOK.md:1178:- VERIFICATION: A hello-stdio + UDP proof cross-built all four targets twice byte-identically with Go 1.26.5; macOS arm64 ran natively and amd64 under Rosetta 2. Native Linux and Intel-Mac release smoke remain mandatory stop-line CI gates because this host had no Linux runtime or Intel hardware. Evidence: `.research/260720_task-260715-3bdplx-relay-language-cross-build-toolchain.md`.
./LOGBOOK.md:1207:- FINDING: Both accepted adapters have real read-lifecycle defects — non-cancellable `withCheckedContinuation` and silent `zip` truncation at Sources/ReluxTunnelMacOSAdapter/MacOSProviderCompositionRoot.swift:19 and Sources/ReluxTunnelIOSAdapter/IOSProviderCompositionRoot.swift:21; gap-closure task TASK-260720-9xy8yx correctly blocks the bridge implementation.
./LOGBOOK.md:1211:- DECISION: ADR-029 fixes one acyclic consumer-to-dependency graph: the containing app owns persisted configuration and activation, the packet-tunnel provider owns live state, thin platform/native/SSH adapters depend inward on platform-neutral `ReluxTunnelCore`, and the harness composes the same package graph. The relay remains a hash-verified Go resource input rather than linked code.
